1
00:00:57,555 --> 00:00:58,890
Well, guys.

2
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:00,308
Condolences in advance.

3
00:01:00,642 --> 00:01:01,434
Asshole.

4
00:01:01,517 --> 00:01:02,452
Dong?

5
00:01:02,477 --> 00:01:04,145
Dong, where are you?

6
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:05,480
Dong?

7
00:01:08,608 --> 00:01:09,692
Have you seen Dong?

8
00:01:09,692 --> 00:01:10,251
Mommy?

9
00:01:10,318 --> 00:01:11,611
He's downstairs.

10
00:01:14,072 --> 00:01:15,490
Who the fuck is that?

11
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:16,491
Who's that?

12
00:01:19,452 --> 00:01:21,996
Whoa, no way. She has
the same name as Mommy!

13
00:01:21,996 --> 00:01:23,956
Fancy meeting you here.

14
00:01:29,087 --> 00:01:30,088
I'm sorry.

15
00:01:30,088 --> 00:01:31,964
I just got emotional.

16
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:34,175
Hey, Dong, want me to
introduce you to my dad too?

17
00:01:34,384 --> 00:01:35,510
I'm not yet ready.

18
00:01:39,806 --> 00:01:40,682
I love you, wife.

19
00:01:40,682 --> 00:01:42,475
I love you so much too, Dong.

20
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:48,523
I want you two to work
together to stop that plan.

21
00:01:48,815 --> 00:01:50,358
I don't care about Roswell.

22
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:53,152
I still want to kill him.

23
00:01:58,241 --> 00:01:59,701
Where's Mr. Ken?

24
00:02:01,285 --> 00:02:02,537
Why isn't he here yet?

25
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:17,802
Why are they wearing masks?

26
00:02:18,803 --> 00:02:20,388
Don't they want
to be recognized?

27
00:02:21,097 --> 00:02:22,098
Come with us.

28
00:02:24,726 --> 00:02:25,893
Is this going to SM North?

29
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:42,326
Why aren't you answering
your phone, Aemie?

30
00:02:48,708 --> 00:02:50,752
Maybe Aemie's phone
just died, Mr. Roswell.

31
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:55,339
You know your wife, she
doesn't like charging her phone.

32
00:03:00,052 --> 00:03:02,180
I have a bad feeling
about this, Lamperouge.

33
00:04:02,824 --> 00:04:04,367
Aren't we going to kill her yet?

34
00:04:05,785 --> 00:04:06,994
Just relax.

35
00:04:07,578 --> 00:04:08,871
We still have something to do.

36
00:04:27,306 --> 00:04:27,974
Oh!

37
00:04:28,349 --> 00:04:30,268
Zeke's an actor now!

38
00:04:30,893 --> 00:04:33,187
Hey, you're awake.

39
00:04:33,563 --> 00:04:34,730
Aren't you scared of us?

40
00:04:37,608 --> 00:04:38,317
Why?

41
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:40,528
Are you ghosts?

42
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:43,739
You crazy woman!

43
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:48,202
You're being so mean to me, sir!

44
00:04:48,661 --> 00:04:50,663
And I'm the crazy one?

45
00:04:52,274 --> 00:04:53,819
You're the ones all covered up.

46
00:04:53,844 --> 00:04:55,668
Even under the scorching sun.

47
00:04:55,668 --> 00:04:57,587
Besides, even if you
didn't cover your faces,

48
00:04:57,587 --> 00:04:59,005
I wouldn't recognize you anyway.

49
00:04:59,353 --> 00:05:00,479
You're crazy!

50
00:05:01,424 --> 00:05:02,352
Ouch!

51
00:05:05,803 --> 00:05:07,722
You're being so mean to me, sir!

52
00:05:09,015 --> 00:05:10,391
What did I ever do to you?

53
00:05:10,391 --> 00:05:12,268
Why did you slap me?

54
00:05:12,476 --> 00:05:13,811
We're members of Yaji.

55
00:05:14,687 --> 00:05:17,064
You owe us a lot!

56
00:05:19,442 --> 00:05:20,318
Yaji?

57
00:05:23,237 --> 00:05:24,238
Is this guy high?

58
00:05:24,822 --> 00:05:28,075
He's not even in any of the
profiles Zeke showed me.

59
00:05:31,537 --> 00:05:32,914
Call her husband.

60
00:05:40,087 --> 00:05:41,172
Zeke!

61
00:05:41,714 --> 00:05:43,090
Here, talk to him.

62
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:43,925
Zeke!

63
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,217
Zeke!

64
00:05:45,217 --> 00:05:45,885
Wife?

65
00:05:46,552 --> 00:05:47,595
Zeke!

66
00:05:47,595 --> 00:05:49,196
Wife, are you listening to me?

67
00:05:49,221 --> 00:05:50,806
Zeke, yes, I'm here!

68
00:05:50,806 --> 00:05:51,994
I'm here!

69
00:05:52,308 --> 00:05:54,018
Did they fucking hurt you, wife?

70
00:05:54,018 --> 00:05:55,227
Yes, Zeke!

71
00:05:55,645 --> 00:05:58,064
Now that you've
heard your wife's voice,

72
00:05:59,106 --> 00:06:02,944
you'll do everything we
tell you to do, Roswell.

73
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:05,863
Zeke!

74
00:06:15,456 --> 00:06:16,457
Everything's ready.

75
00:06:16,457 --> 00:06:18,167
The bomb is already planted.

76
00:06:18,167 --> 00:06:20,044
He'll surely be
dead in a little while.

77
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,837
Bomb?

78
00:06:22,254 --> 00:06:23,839
There, it's almost time!

79
00:06:27,134 --> 00:06:29,512
This is the end for you, Roswell!

80
00:06:31,055 --> 00:06:31,722
Zeke!

81
00:06:31,722 --> 00:06:32,639
Zeke!

82
00:06:34,725 --> 00:06:35,893
Get out of there, Zeke!

83
00:06:36,352 --> 00:06:37,478
Sir!

84
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:39,397
Keep quiet! We're watching, okay!

85
00:06:39,397 --> 00:06:40,064
Sir!

86
00:06:40,064 --> 00:06:40,731
Sir!

87
00:06:40,731 --> 00:06:43,359
Please don't do it, sir!

88
00:06:43,526 --> 00:06:45,152
Please don't do it!

89
00:06:45,152 --> 00:06:47,196
Sir, just kill me instead.

90
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:48,114
Just me!

91
00:06:48,114 --> 00:06:49,156
Just kill me, sir, ple—

92
00:06:49,156 --> 00:06:50,091
Shut up!

93
00:06:50,116 --> 00:06:51,158
Just me!

94
00:06:51,826 --> 00:06:52,840
I love—

95
00:06:53,528 --> 00:06:55,196
Zeke!

96
00:06:55,454 --> 00:06:57,415
Bye, Roswell!

97
00:06:59,041 --> 00:07:01,002
- Zeke!
- Dead!

98
00:07:04,255 --> 00:07:05,064
What?

99
00:07:05,089 --> 00:07:06,424
Now that your husband is dead,

100
00:07:07,633 --> 00:07:09,677
you're next!

101
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:14,432
You guys are terrible!

102
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:26,235
This can't be.

103
00:07:27,737 --> 00:07:29,697
Zeke can't be gone.

104
00:07:29,822 --> 00:07:31,532
It can't be.

105
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:38,289
You killed my husband.

106
00:09:55,259 --> 00:09:56,427
Too thick.

107
00:09:57,094 --> 00:09:58,262
Give me something thinner.

108
00:09:58,470 --> 00:09:59,613
Thinner.

109
00:09:59,638 --> 00:10:00,595
Here, Seb.

110
00:10:05,436 --> 00:10:07,479
Looks like it's about to
be defused, Mr. Roswell.

111
00:10:08,314 --> 00:10:09,438
Lee, update.

112
00:10:13,194 --> 00:10:14,128
Got it.

113
00:10:14,153 --> 00:10:15,259
Here, boss.

114
00:10:15,529 --> 00:10:16,595
The move is ready.

115
00:10:20,868 --> 00:10:22,953
This is the end
for you, Roswell!

116
00:10:24,538 --> 00:10:26,582
- Zeke!
- Dead!

117
00:10:28,334 --> 00:10:30,544
When my wife's kidnappers call,

118
00:10:30,794 --> 00:10:32,421
play this video for them.

119
00:10:32,546 --> 00:10:33,380
Copy, boss.

120
00:10:35,716 --> 00:10:36,383
Woo!

121
00:10:40,888 --> 00:10:42,181
It's defused, boss.

122
00:10:42,598 --> 00:10:43,265
Good.

123
00:10:43,849 --> 00:10:44,683
Let's go, Lee.

124
00:10:45,142 --> 00:10:46,602
Send me Aemie's location.

125
00:10:46,602 --> 00:10:47,353
Okay, boss.

126
00:11:23,347 --> 00:11:23,973
Aemie!

127
00:12:23,490 --> 00:12:24,527
Dong?

128
00:12:25,701 --> 00:12:27,737
Dong, I thought you were dead.

129
00:12:27,870 --> 00:12:28,816
Dong.

130
00:12:35,669 --> 00:12:36,605
Boss.

131
00:12:37,963 --> 00:12:39,173
We'll go ahead.

132
00:12:46,972 --> 00:12:47,890
How—

133
00:12:48,474 --> 00:12:49,558
How did—

134
00:12:50,059 --> 00:12:51,560
How are you alive?!

135
00:12:51,935 --> 00:12:53,645
I saw the explosion earlier...

136
00:12:54,813 --> 00:12:56,065
It wasn't me.

137
00:12:59,026 --> 00:13:00,194
What do you mean,
"it wasn't you?"

138
00:13:00,194 --> 00:13:00,861
It was you.

139
00:13:00,861 --> 00:13:01,987
I saw it.

140
00:13:03,113 --> 00:13:04,406
It was planned.

141
00:13:07,493 --> 00:13:08,660
It's hard to explain.

142
00:13:09,244 --> 00:13:10,746
I'm sure you'll never get it.

143
00:13:14,083 --> 00:13:15,959
Does he think I'm slow?

144
00:13:20,005 --> 00:13:21,173
Okay, fine.

145
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:28,180
Oh, my god!

146
00:13:29,181 --> 00:13:29,807
Dong!

147
00:13:30,057 --> 00:13:30,933
It was Mr. Ken!

148
00:13:30,933 --> 00:13:33,060
Maybe he's still at the restaurant!

149
00:13:34,269 --> 00:13:35,979
He wasn't the one
who texted you.

150
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:39,583
It was...

151
00:13:39,608 --> 00:13:41,985
It was—J.K. Blood.

152
00:13:41,985 --> 00:13:43,904
Wasn't it Jerson Ken Blood?

153
00:13:44,196 --> 00:13:46,740
Oh, it was Mr. Ken, Dong.

154
00:13:46,907 --> 00:13:50,911
I talked to him the moment I found
out that you went out for lunch with him.

155
00:13:53,872 --> 00:13:55,833
Who texted me?

156
00:13:57,918 --> 00:13:59,711
Someone pretending to be Jerson.

157
00:14:00,421 --> 00:14:01,672
To kidnap you.

158
00:14:10,973 --> 00:14:12,015
Oh!

159
00:14:12,224 --> 00:14:13,267
Oh!

160
00:14:15,644 --> 00:14:16,103
Does—

161
00:14:16,103 --> 00:14:17,187
Does anything hurt?

162
00:14:17,396 --> 00:14:19,314
No!

163
00:14:19,731 --> 00:14:21,108
No!

164
00:14:21,108 --> 00:14:22,025
No!

165
00:14:22,025 --> 00:14:23,026
What is it?!

166
00:14:25,529 --> 00:14:26,358
What?

167
00:14:28,323 --> 00:14:30,367
What a waste of the
two-peso load I sent.

168
00:14:30,367 --> 00:14:32,077
It wasn't even Mr. Ken.

169
00:14:40,566 --> 00:14:41,859
Why are you laughing?

170
00:14:43,822 --> 00:14:45,699
Do you have something
to tell me, Dong?

171
00:14:46,675 --> 00:14:47,634
Wife.

172
00:14:50,095 --> 00:14:51,847
You did something very bad.

173
00:15:01,565 --> 00:15:02,733
Zeke.

174
00:15:04,318 --> 00:15:06,528
What happened to those men?

175
00:15:08,113 --> 00:15:09,198
They're all dead.

176
00:15:16,038 --> 00:15:17,498
I did that?

177
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,670
I'm sorry I was too
late to protect you.

178
00:15:26,715 --> 00:15:28,509
You ended up killing them.

179
00:15:34,348 --> 00:15:36,350
Zeke, I didn't mean to.

180
00:15:37,184 --> 00:15:38,477
I didn't mean to.

181
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:42,147
I thought you were dead,
and everything just went dark.

182
00:15:42,147 --> 00:15:43,273
I know.

183
00:15:44,233 --> 00:15:46,401
I should've been the
one to do that, not you.

184
00:15:47,653 --> 00:15:49,655
I'm supposed to be
the bad person here.

185
00:15:56,119 --> 00:15:57,329
Zeke.

186
00:16:00,165 --> 00:16:02,000
Thank you for taking care of me

187
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,002
and protecting me.

188
00:16:04,336 --> 00:16:08,048
But just like you, I also want
to protect the people I love.

189
00:16:08,549 --> 00:16:09,675
And you're one of them.

190
00:16:10,259 --> 00:16:11,301
But...

191
00:16:12,719 --> 00:16:13,971
But I'm just scared.

192
00:16:13,971 --> 00:16:14,721
Why...

193
00:16:15,973 --> 00:16:18,141
don't I feel guilty?

194
00:16:19,768 --> 00:16:21,228
Am I a bad person now, Dong?

195
00:16:39,079 --> 00:16:40,455
Don't leave me, Zeke.

196
00:16:40,455 --> 00:16:41,707
Please?

197
00:16:43,417 --> 00:16:44,334
I won't.

198
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:46,253
I won't think of leaving you.

199
00:16:48,255 --> 00:16:49,715
Unless you want me to.

200
00:16:57,931 --> 00:16:59,266
Why are you laughing?

201
00:16:59,683 --> 00:17:00,517
You know what?

202
00:17:01,184 --> 00:17:02,811
I should kiss you more often.

203
00:17:04,021 --> 00:17:06,732
It knocks some sense
into you every time I do.

204
00:17:08,734 --> 00:17:09,318
You're right.

205
00:17:09,318 --> 00:17:10,861
I feel like it'll be weird—

206
00:18:35,153 --> 00:18:36,405
You can't leave, wife.

207
00:18:37,114 --> 00:18:37,964
Huh?

208
00:18:37,989 --> 00:18:38,906
Why?

209
00:18:39,533 --> 00:18:40,951
You still need to rest.

210
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,036
I'm fine now.

211
00:18:44,413 --> 00:18:45,706
I said rest.

212
00:18:46,832 --> 00:18:47,708
Dong.

213
00:18:47,708 --> 00:18:49,334
I've been lying
down all afternoon.

214
00:18:49,334 --> 00:18:52,421
Besides, I'm not tired, so I
don't need to rest anymore.

215
00:19:08,103 --> 00:19:09,024
Hey.

216
00:19:09,813 --> 00:19:10,731
Come on, Dong.

217
00:19:11,231 --> 00:19:13,900
I'm not allowed to go out, and
now you're taking my phone too?

218
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:15,902
I'll answer it while you rest.

219
00:19:24,298 --> 00:19:27,760
Baby Ae, I'm outside your house.

220
00:19:28,707 --> 00:19:29,833
Mrs. Romero.

221
00:19:30,459 --> 00:19:32,853
Zeke? Why did you answer?

222
00:19:33,229 --> 00:19:34,271
Where's Aemie?

223
00:19:34,296 --> 00:19:35,338
She's resting.

224
00:19:36,465 --> 00:19:37,524
Mrs. Romero.

225
00:19:38,216 --> 00:19:39,384
We have to talk.

226
00:19:39,384 --> 00:19:41,052
Talk about what?

227
00:19:42,929 --> 00:19:44,891
I'll be there in a while.

228
00:20:37,901 --> 00:20:39,694
I still can't believe it.

229
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:41,571
I can't accept it.

230
00:20:44,366 --> 00:20:46,117
My twin is dead.

231
00:20:46,368 --> 00:20:47,577
Shan is dead.

232
00:20:50,956 --> 00:20:51,754
I can't—

233
00:20:52,082 --> 00:20:53,667
I don't understand it either.

234
00:20:56,503 --> 00:20:57,754
First, Nico.

235
00:20:59,464 --> 00:21:00,924
Now, Venice.

236
00:21:03,301 --> 00:21:05,595
What's happening to our friends?

237
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:08,265
I don't know anymore.

238
00:21:17,649 --> 00:21:18,479
Sir.

239
00:21:19,526 --> 00:21:21,570
Do you have any leads
on who killed my twin?

240
00:21:22,195 --> 00:21:23,405
Not yet, sir.

241
00:21:25,407 --> 00:21:26,424
My condolences.

242
00:21:28,994 --> 00:21:30,120
Louie.

243
00:21:30,328 --> 00:21:31,997
We'll find out the truth.

244
00:21:32,539 --> 00:21:33,999
The truth will come out.

245
00:21:44,551 --> 00:21:45,844
Condolences, Louie.

246
00:21:51,016 --> 00:21:52,017
Stay here for now, okay?

247
00:21:52,434 --> 00:21:53,435
You'll come back, right?

248
00:21:53,435 --> 00:21:54,644
I will.

249
00:21:57,856 --> 00:21:58,849
Just stay here.

250
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:13,204
What about Aemie girl?

251
00:22:14,748 --> 00:22:16,458
I've been calling
her since yesterday.

252
00:22:16,583 --> 00:22:17,959
I can't reach her.

253
00:22:18,919 --> 00:22:20,086
I'm getting worried.

254
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:30,764
I thought you had a plan.

255
00:22:32,390 --> 00:22:34,351
Was this because of Auntie?

256
00:22:36,770 --> 00:22:38,605
I should ask her if
she knows something.

257
00:22:40,774 --> 00:22:41,849
What is it, Cai?

258
00:22:42,359 --> 00:22:42,901
Huh?

259
00:22:42,901 --> 00:22:44,027
Are you saying something?

260
00:22:44,194 --> 00:22:45,162
Nothing.

261
00:22:45,779 --> 00:22:47,072
I'm just going to the bathroom.

262
00:22:47,739 --> 00:22:48,615
Excuse me.

263
00:23:03,129 --> 00:23:04,256
Where's my daughter?

264
00:23:06,257 --> 00:23:07,384
She's upstairs.

265
00:23:10,136 --> 00:23:11,513
We need to talk first.

266
00:23:12,347 --> 00:23:13,848
Something happened yesterday.

267
00:23:14,391 --> 00:23:15,517
Yes, I heard.

268
00:23:16,184 --> 00:23:17,185
Have you also heard,

269
00:23:17,602 --> 00:23:19,562
that she killed those
who kidnapped her?

270
00:23:20,814 --> 00:23:21,690
What?

271
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:23,024
Aemie?

272
00:23:24,359 --> 00:23:26,486
They introduced themselves
as members of Yaji.

273
00:23:26,486 --> 00:23:27,362
Yaji?

274
00:23:28,697 --> 00:23:29,698
Impossible.

275
00:23:30,448 --> 00:23:32,242
I know how Yaji operates.

276
00:23:33,702 --> 00:23:34,619
See this?

277
00:23:51,302 --> 00:23:54,097
Who would send this to Baby Ae?

278
00:23:55,181 --> 00:23:56,516
Well, it says Yaji.

279
00:23:57,434 --> 00:24:00,020
It was given to my
wife over a month ago.

280
00:24:00,145 --> 00:24:01,396
Does my daughter know?

281
00:24:03,314 --> 00:24:04,024
Good.

282
00:24:04,482 --> 00:24:05,692
Even Shan Venice's death,

283
00:24:06,526 --> 00:24:08,028
I haven't told her yet.

284
00:24:08,611 --> 00:24:10,530
I think she needs to know.

285
00:24:10,905 --> 00:24:13,700
But she doesn't need
to know the whole truth.

286
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,660
She's her friend too.

287
00:24:15,994 --> 00:24:17,287
She might get hurt.

288
00:24:19,164 --> 00:24:21,082
